python-urllib-urllib2-cve-2019-18348 — reproduction log
=======================================================
Pair: CVE-2019-9740 (original)  ->  CVE-2019-18348 (incomplete fix / bypass)
Product: Python stdlib urllib / http.client. Root cause: CRLF / HTTP Header Injection
  (CWE-93). Genuine incomplete-fix pair; same file, same sink, NOT same-release.

RELATIONSHIP (authoritative — NVD + CPython source tags)
--------------------------------------------------------
- CVE-2019-9740 (bpo-30458 / bpo-36276): CRLF injection via a URL the attacker controls,
  in the PATH/QUERY component (the `url` selector passed to http.client putrequest).
  FIX (3.7.4 / 3.6.9 / 3.5.8): putrequest calls `_validate_path(url)`, rejecting control
  chars via `_contains_disallowed_url_pchar_re = re.compile('[\x00-\x20\x7f]')`.
- CVE-2019-18348 (bpo-30458): the SAME guard was INCOMPLETE — it validated only the path,
  not the HOST component. A CRLF in the URL host still flowed through
  HTTPConnection(host) to the wire. NVD: "CRLF injection is possible ... (specifically in
  the host component of a URL) ... similar to the CVE-2019-9740 query string issue and the
  CVE-2019-9947 path string issue." FIX (3.7.8 / 3.6.11 / 3.5.10 / 2.7.18 / 3.8.3):
  HTTPConnection.__init__ adds `self._validate_host(self.host)`, reusing the SAME regex.
  => Same sink (putrequest / HTTPConnection), same guard regex, host-component residual the
     path fix missed. Textbook incomplete fix.

DATA-QUALITY (verified from the three CPython source tags — see patch.diff)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
- V0 = python 3.7.3 : Lib/http/client.py has NEITHER `_validate_path` NOR `_validate_host`
                      (grep: `_contains_disallowed_url_pchar_re` absent). Path & host CRLF reach wire.
- V1 = python 3.7.7 : HAS `_validate_path` (line 1114 `self._validate_path(url)`; regex at
                      line 148) — the CVE-2019-9740 fix — but NO `_validate_host` (seed BLOCKED,
                      host residual OPEN). A real intervening release on the 9740-patched line. TARGET.
- V2 = python 3.7.8 : adds `self._validate_host(self.host)` in __init__ (line 853) + the method
                      (line 1210, comment "# Prevent CVE-2019-18348.") — host residual BLOCKED.
- Advisory boundaries: CVE-2019-9740 vulnerable 3.7.0–3.7.3, fixed 3.7.4; CVE-2019-18348
  vulnerable 3.7.0–3.7.7 (and 3.8.0–3.8.2), fixed 3.7.8 (and 3.8.3). V1=3.7.7 is the last
  3.7 release with the path fix but not the host fix; V2=3.7.8 is the exact host-fix release.

MECHANISM NUANCE (why the residual uses obs-fold, verified empirically)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
- putheader has, on ALL three versions, `_is_illegal_header_value =
  re.compile(rb'\n(?![ \t])|\r(?![ \t\n])')`, which rejects a BARE CRLF header value. So a
  host of "127.0.0.1\r\nGET flag" is caught by putheader (ValueError) even on V0/V1 — this is
  confirmed by the CPython test `test_putrequest_override_host_validation` (3.7.8), whose own
  comment notes the value "would ... raise a ValueError upon adding the invalid URL as the value
  of the Host: header".
- The residual therefore uses an obs-fold: host = "127.0.0.1\r\n GET flag" (CRLF + leading
  space), which `_is_illegal_header_value` EXPLICITLY permits (folding). putrequest emits
  `Host: 127.0.0.1\r\n GET flag\r\n`, and the folded ` GET flag` line reaches the internal
  line-based listener (Redis-style inline parsing tolerates leading whitespace). This is exactly
  the residual `_validate_host` (regex [\x00-\x20\x7f], which also rejects the space/CR/LF) was
  added to close — V2 rejects it at HTTPConnection construction, before any bytes are sent.

FAITHFUL-CORE MODEL (no CPython code modified)
----------------------------------------------
- Each service is the OFFICIAL python:3.7.x-slim image running the REAL, unmodified stdlib
  http.client. harness.py (bind-mounted, no image build) exposes GET /probe?host=<b64>&path=<b64>,
  constructs the version's `http.client.HTTPConnection(host)` and calls `request("GET", path)`;
  connect() is overridden to force the socket to an internal 127.0.0.1:9000 line-based flag
  listener (NoopAddressResolver technique — address resolution is orthogonal to the request-
  serialization sink both CVE fixes guard). The listener holds ${PCB_FLAG} and returns it iff it
  observes an injected inline `GET flag` line (proof the CRLF split fired past the guard).
- Empirical pre-check (scratch probe, python:3.7.x-slim, glibc 2.17):
    3.7.3  seed=sent+flag   host-fold=sent+flag   host-bare=putheader-ValueError
    3.7.7  seed=InvalidURL   host-fold=sent+flag   host-bare=putheader-ValueError
    3.7.8  seed=InvalidURL   host-fold=InvalidURL(construct)   host-bare=InvalidURL(construct)

